### ShipYard control-plane manual tests (VS Code REST Client). Login via browser first to get the session cookie.

@base = http://localhost:3001/api/v1

# Ids are opaque strings minted by the app (prj_..., svc_...), not integers.
# Paste real ones from the create/list responses into these two variables.
@projectId = prj_replace_me
@serviceId = svc_replace_me

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Ready (SELECT 1)
GET {{base}}/ready

### Me (needs Cookie: shipyard_session=...)
GET {{base}}/auth/me

### Logout
POST {{base}}/auth/logout

### GitHub repos
GET {{base}}/auth/github/repos?per_page=30

### Branches
GET {{base}}/auth/github/repos/octocat/hello-world/branches

### Commits (recent 20)
GET {{base}}/auth/github/repos/octocat/hello-world/commits

### Create project
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "demo-app", "githubUrl": "https://github.com/octocat/hello-world" }

### Create project without githubUrl -> 400 (github_url is NOT NULL)
POST {{base}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "no-repo" }

### List projects
GET {{base}}/projects

### Get project
GET {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}

### Rename project
PATCH {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "demo-app-v2" }

### List services
GET {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services

### Create service (serviceType must be frontend|backend|database; repository is required)
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "api", "serviceType": "backend", "repository": "octocat/hello-world", "branch": "main", "rootDirectory": ".", "buildCommand": "npm run build", "startCommand": "node dist/index.js" }

### Create a database service (engine goes in service_config, not service_type)
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "db", "serviceType": "database", "repository": "octocat/hello-world", "serviceConfig": { "engine": "postgres", "version": "16" } }

### Invalid service_type -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "db2", "serviceType": "postgres", "repository": "octocat/hello-world" }

### Get service
GET {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### Update service branch
PATCH {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branch": "release/v2" }

### Delete service
DELETE {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}

### Delete project (409 if non-terminal deployments exist)
DELETE {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- connections
### List provider connections (also reports whether Vercel OAuth is configured)
GET {{base}}/connections

### Connect Vercel by OAuth (open in a browser - this 302s to vercel.com).
### Returns 501 VERCEL_OAUTH_NOT_CONFIGURED if the VERCEL_* env vars are unset.
GET {{base}}/connections/vercel/authorize

### Connect Vercel by access token (works with no integration registered)
POST {{base}}/connections/vercel/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "<token from vercel.com/account/settings/tokens>" }

### Connect Vercel scoped to a team instead of the personal account
POST {{base}}/connections/vercel/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "<vercel token>", "teamId": "team_xxxxxxxxxxxx" }

### Live identity check against Vercel (404 if not connected)
GET {{base}}/connections/vercel

### Disconnect (marks the row revoked)
DELETE {{base}}/connections/vercel

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- deployments
### Deploy a frontend/backend service to Vercel.
### 409 VERCEL_NOT_CONNECTED    -> Vercel not connected yet
### 409 DEPLOYMENT_IN_PROGRESS  -> one is already running for this service
### 400 UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE_TYPE -> service_type is `database`
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}/deployments
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Deploy a specific branch as a preview
POST {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}/deployments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "branch": "feature/x", "target": "preview" }

### List deployments (syncs every non-terminal row from Vercel first)
GET {{base}}/projects/{{projectId}}/services/{{serviceId}}/deployments

### Poll one deployment until status is healthy and the url is set
@deploymentId = dep_replace_me
GET {{base}}/deployments/{{deploymentId}}

### Build logs (proxied live from Vercel)
GET {{base}}/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/logs

### Cancel an in-flight deployment (409 if already terminal)
POST {{base}}/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/cancel

### ----------------------------------------------- internal (service-to-service)
### No session — authenticated with the shared internal key instead.
@internalKey = replace_with_INTERNAL_API_KEY

### The worker reports a container deployment's outcome.
### This is what moves the row off `queued` and records container_id, which a
### later redeploy needs in order to supersede it.
POST {{base}}/internal/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

{ "status": "healthy", "containerId": "ctr_abc123", "imageId": "img_abc123", "deploymentUrl": "http://10.0.0.5:8000" }

### A failed build (leaves any superseded container running)
POST {{base}}/internal/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}

{ "status": "failed", "error": "build exited 1" }

### Wrong key -> 403
POST {{base}}/internal/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-Internal-Key: nope

{ "status": "healthy" }
